TY  - JOUR
TI  - AI-Recipe Recommendation System
AU  - Abhishek H. B.
AU  - P. Mallya
AU  - P. C. Hiremath
AU  - Swarnatama Ganguli
AU  - S. Pradeep
AU  - Prashanth Kannadaguli
PY  - 2025
JO  - 2025 International Conference on Advances in Next-Gen Computer Science
(ICANCS)
AB  - The development and deployment of a deep learning (DL) and machine
learning (ML)-based recipe recommendation system techniques to make
recipe recommendations based on user-available ingredients is
presented in this project. With the increasing complexity of meal
planning and the wide variety of Indian and international cuisines,
people frequently don't understand what they are capable of producing
with certain or limited ingredient. To overcome this difficulty, the
system makes use of a dataset of more than 59,000 recipes that has
been enhanced by preprocessing procedures such ingredient
standardization, data cleaning, normalization, and duplicate removal.
TF-IDF, word2vec and glove embeddings were among the methods used to
extract features, logistic regressions, k-nearest neighbors, and
XGboost, as well as CNN-style deep learning algorithms, LSTM, and
transformer-based architectures, were assessed. Transformer models
outperformed the others in terms of accurately and contextually aware
recipe prediction. To help accommodate user time constraints, recipes
were separated into three as well. preparations time bins, Quick (less
than 30 minutes), medium (30 to 60 minutes), and long (more than 60
minutes), A streamlit- based web application was created to guarantee
real-world applicability, users may enter ingredients and instantly
obtain recipe recommendations and preparation instructions. The
absence of dietary choice and allergy considerations is Among the
system's present drawbacks, but it also improves user convenience,
reduces food waste and encourages effective ingredient use. Overall,
by providing individualized, effective and sustainable meal
recommendations, the study demonstrates how AI-driven solutions have
the potential to revolutionize everyday cooking.
DO  - 10.1109/ICANCS65819.2025.11376688
UR  - https://www.semanticscholar.org/paper/b7d599cde08b39841e3a5b0457bce438d3160ea3
